    "narrative": "For tonight\u2019s slate, our lineup is anchored by **Lawrence Butler**, who provides the highest utility at a score of 74.61. Batting lead-off against Lowder (xERA 4.74), **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a massive 10% boost due to his spot in the order and a favorable 13% platoon adjustment. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) and **JJ Bleday** (68.50) are elite starts; **Jonathan Aranda** draws a soft matchup against Sugano (xERA 5.02) while **JJ Bleday** enjoys a 19% boost from facing a struggling Lopez. **Bryce Harper** (70.37) remains our premier power threat, as he faces Irvin with a strong 0.387 xwOBA projection, providing the stability we need to hunt for R and RBI totals.\n\nThe most difficult benching decision involved **Gleyber Torres** (39.86), who missed our 40.0 floor by the narrowest of margins. Despite a favorable batting order position, his output is capped by a difficult matchup against Woo and a negative platoon dynamic that neutralized his base projection. Meanwhile, we are closely monitoring the bottom of the order: **Justin Crawford** (57.03) serves as our primary speed source, though he is slightly hampered by an 8% penalty for hitting ninth. We have opted to sit **Jung Hoo Lee** (39.10), as his score was depressed by a lack of opposing SP vulnerability and a platoon disadvantage that makes him a liability for today\u2019s specific category targets.\n\nFrom a tactical perspective, keep a close eye on **Cal Raleigh** (41.14) and **Brendan Donovan** (42.87). Both are hovering near our \"Marginal\" threshold due to the challenging matchup against Anderson, who features an elite 3.15 xERA. While their efficiency scores are low, we are maintaining their starts to preserve our game caps, though they represent the highest volatility in our lineup today. Ensure **Yainer Diaz** (55.00) remains in the mix; despite his #8 hole, he is well-positioned to capitalize on a favorable park factor and a mid-tier outing from Taillon. We continue to hold **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** on the bench due to his absence from today's active lineup, and we are proceeding without **Will Smith**, who remains on the IL.",
